{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report", "label": "Task 8 Report: Port the homepage page-specific behaviours", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report_porting_rules_table", "label": "Task 5 porting-rules table (verbatim JS-to-TS behaviour port)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every ported line must trace to a table row (root deletion, cleanups array, disposer wrapper, prop substitution) or a zero-runtime-effect TS typing accommodation; selectors, thresholds, easings and durations are never changed, so inefficiencies and dead code are ported as written and reported."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report_initfanpointer_dead_code", "label": "initFanPointer dead method (never called, [data-ag-fan] markup absent)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dead two independent ways in the original artifact; initially ported and wired per instruction, then deleted in Fix Round 1 (fanPointer.ts removed from lib/behaviors and HOME_MODULES)."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report_componentdidmount_order", "label": "componentDidMount call order as module-list source of truth", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Page module lists are derived by filtering the original componentDidMount call order to non-SHARED calls, rather than trusting the brief."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report_window_resources_poster_gap", "label": "initVideo lightbox poster depends on window.__resources", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bundler resource table has no equivalent in the Next.js app, so data-vt-poster rendered literal assets/*.jpg paths; root-caused upstream to __bundler/ext_resources never being read by unbundle.mjs, rather than improvising a map in video.ts."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report_ext_resources_json", "label": ".source/ext-resources.json (ext_resources id -> public path map)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Written by tools/unbundle.mjs from each bundle's __bundler/ext_resources block; convert.mjs rewrites assets/<id>.<ext> references through it and reports unmapped ones as problems."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report_ether_dead_flag_teardown", "label": "Dead-flag disposer for async dynamic import (ether/stroke teardown)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Returned disposer sets dead=true and calls dispose?.(); the import().then callback bails if dead, so unmount-before-import-resolves never creates a WebGL context, and liquid-ether/stroke-text idempotent disposers make double-invocation safe."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report_dynamic_import_code_split", "label": "Dynamic import() keeps three.js/GSAP out of First Load JS", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "three.js/liquid-ether (~472 KB) and gsap/stroke-text chunks load lazily and are not counted in the home route First Load JS."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report_reel_dead_q_computation", "label": "reel.ts dead 'q' computation (ported verbatim, reported)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "q is computed and never read, and its entity regex can never match since getAttribute returns decoded text; kept per the no-removal-on-own-judgement policy."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report_disposal_audit_timer_gaps", "label": "Disposal audit: uncleared one-off timers in video/trail/reel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pre-existing, source-identical cosmetic gaps (setTimeout inside callbacks never cleared on unmount); deliberately not fixed per porting mandate."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report_cursor_appends_to_body", "label": "initCursor appends dot to document.body, not root", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Root has overflow-clip and parallax-transformed descendants, either of which would break a position:fixed cursor overlay; kept as faithful and necessary."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report_mutation_proof_testing", "label": "Mutation-proof testing (break the fix, confirm the new test fails)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "New tests are only trusted after removing the fix and observing exactly the new tests fail, then restoring; proves tests are not vacuous."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report_trail_null_guard", "label": "trail.ts combined null-guard mirroring initShell idiom", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only deviation adding control flow; required by strict null checks and copied from the same file's own initShell precedent; unreachable in practice."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report", "target": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report_porting_rules_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report", "target": "lib_behaviors_services", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report", "target": "lib_behaviors_hovers", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report", "target": "lib_behaviors_cursor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_8_report", "target": "lib_behaviors_flags", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-8-report.md", "source_l